{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/674868-writing-your-legend-society-s-reaction-to-a-beast","id":674868,"title":"Writing Your Legend - Society's Reaction to a Beast?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-22T20:18:33-07:00","id":674868,"title":"Writing Your Legend - Society's Reaction to a Beast?","content":"I've been playing with the idea of &quot;writing your legend&quot; on the World of Darkness. Of what it takes to have kids tell ghost stories about you, to force society to change in response to your hunts, to be the next Wolf (from <i>Little Red Riding Hood</i>).<br /> <br /> In keeping with that idea, do we have rules for the social consequences of a Beast's predation? Provoking Heroes is an obvious one . . .but what about the rest of society? What does it take to launch a police (or mob!) task force? Catch the eye of other supernaturals? To get reforms passed into law?<br /> <br /> Consider the consequences of Feeding with a particular bent. Suppose a Nemesis starts focusing on the local drug dealers - how long/many/spectacular Feedings are necessary to start making an impact? Dealers shifting out of the neighborhood, drug prices rising, societal conditions improving . . . angry vampires looking for the bastard screwing with the drug trade?<br /> <br /> Or a Collector - how many rare items do they need to acquire before rumors of their hoard start spreading? At what point do mages try to steal the rare grimoires from the Beast's library? Or supernatural thieves start drooling for the dragon's hoard of gold?<br /> <br /> If a Beast with a Hunger for Ruin starts burning down museums, how does society react? And when a Beast tries to feed at higher satiety (and thus needs to get more extreme) . . . What provokes the greatest reaction? Sending severed heads to local dignitaries? Or leaving horrifically mutilated corpses for reporters to find? How drastically can a Tyrant Feed before there are riots (or revolutions!) in the street?<br /> <br /> Just something I'm playing around. And if we don't have formal rules (yet), does anyone have any suggestions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:59:08-07:00","id":674912,"title":"","content":"I have a persistent thought of a Beast, a Tyrant, doing what the example character Boleslav did, but on a larger scale; actually flat-out conquer a city, or even a small country. He could leave his Beast side as a surprise trump card, or just flat-out have it out in the open, if he's got the populace sufficiently cowed.<br /> <br /> On a smaller scale, he could dominate a subset of society, like all the organized crime in a country, or be the military's top general and greatest weapon, or have everyone in a corporation know that they're working for a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T22:10:34-07:00","id":674941,"title":"","content":"An exceedingly lucky Beast could go all Mr. Kurtz on a given region, make himself king by bringing terror and disruption. The trick is keeping the riots, Hero-led or otherwise, from overwhelming the plot. Usually, you save that for either a climax, or a well-timed detour, especially if the Heroes or monsters responsible aren't main antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}